# TOOLS.md — Scribe's WordPress Environment

Copy this file to `TOOLS.md` and fill in your real credentials:

```bash
cp TOOLS.md.example TOOLS.md
```

---

## WordPress Site

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| **Site URL** | `YOUR_WORDPRESS_SITE_URL` |
| **API Base** | `YOUR_WORDPRESS_SITE_URL/wp-json/wp/v2` |
| **Username** | `YOUR_WP_USERNAME` |
| **App Password** | `YOUR_WP_APP_PASSWORD` |
| **Category ID** | `17` (Latest News — adjust for your site) |
| **Post Status** | `draft` (default). Use `--status publish` on the script for live publish. |

Also update `skills/wordpress/publish.sh` and `wp_post_actions.sh` with the same values.

---

## Article & Image (from pipeline run)

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `/tmp/crypto-article.md` | The article written by the Writer agent |
| `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` | The feature image generated by the Creator agent |

---

## Output Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/tmp/wp-result.txt` | WordPress post URL on success |
| `/tmp/wp-error.log` | Exact error reason on failure |

---

## Skill Scripts

### `publish.sh` — create new posts (pipeline Step 6)

```
~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh
```

### `wp_post_actions.sh` — update existing posts (Telegram editorial)

```
~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/wp_post_actions.sh
```

Authors for Telegram publish: see `workspace-orchestrator/config/wp_authors.json`.
